WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
FormalSLT: machine-checked statistical learning in Lean.

00:05.000 --> 00:09.500
VC theory, Rademacher complexity, chaining,
PAC-Bayes, sequential inference, and dependent data.

00:09.500 --> 00:14.000
One stack connecting capacity, complexity,
selection, time, and dependence.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.500
VC growth bounds and metric entropy
feed complexity estimates.

00:18.500 --> 00:23.000
Two checked routes: a VC tail bound
and a metric-entropy integral bound.

00:23.000 --> 00:27.500
PAC-Bayes prices posterior selection
with relative entropy.

00:27.500 --> 00:32.000
One event covers every allowed posterior;
the bound fails with probability at most delta.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.500
Confidence sequences and e-processes
remain valid under repeated looks.

00:36.500 --> 00:41.000
One event covers every time and every declared choice;
an e-process exceeds 1/alpha with probability at most alpha.

00:41.000 --> 00:45.500
Choose from the observed prefix.
Fix the score before the next state.

00:45.500 --> 00:50.000
With a supplied invariant law and Poisson potential,
the correction connects path evidence to stationary risk.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.500
One controlled-queue case study: 4,608 coordinates
reduce to one hit rate, p = (1 + 23 gamma) / 24.

00:54.500 --> 00:59.000
Row TV equals the hit-rate gap inside
the declared family; this is not a membership test.

00:59.000 --> 01:03.000
Four checked declarations, by name: VC ERM, metric
entropy, anytime PAC-Bayes, adaptive trajectories.

01:03.000 --> 01:06.000
Declarations and files are pinned at 501fee4;
the queue is one application of the library.

01:06.000 --> 01:12.000
FormalSLT: a Lean foundation for statistical learning
and modern finite-sample inference.
